      "answer_words": 125,
      "answer": "I'm WeldScope, a research assistant for friction stir welding (FSW). I help explore welding defects, possible causes, process parameters, and corrective actions.\n\nMy bundled document collection contains fsw_doc1.pdf, fsw_doc2.pdf, fsw_doc3.pdf, fsw_doc4.pdf, fsw_doc5.pdf. I combine keyword search (BM25) with semantic vector search, rerank the passages, and pass relevant evidence to a language model to write an answer with source passages. RAG means retrieval-augmented generation: the documents are searched at question time; they aren't used to train the model.\n\nThere's also a bundled example sensor CSV, used when you ask about sensor readings; it isn't a live feed. I use recent completed exchanges for follow-ups within this session. Clear Conversation resets that context.\n\nTry: What causes tunnel defects in FSW? or What do the sensor readings show?",
